{
    "id": "task2",
    "chapterId": "ch_11",
    "title": "Custom Input with v-model and Validation",
    "description": "Create a custom text input component that supports v-model and displays validation errors.",
    "estimatedMinutes": 10,
    "problemStatement": "## Problem Statement\n\nCreate a reusable `ValidatedInput` component that:\n- Accepts `label` (string), `modelValue` (string), and optional `rules` (object with validation functions).\n- Renders an `<input>` bound to `modelValue` via `v-model`.\n- Displays a validation error message if the value is invalid.\n- Emits an `update:modelValue` event.\n- Optionally, accept a `type` prop (text, email, password).\n\nIn the parent component, use this component to build a registration form with fields: username (required, min 3), email (required, valid email), password (required, min 6).\n\nShow submit button disabled until all fields are valid.",
    "hints": [
        "Define the component with `props: ['modelValue', 'label', 'rules', 'type']` and `emits: ['update:modelValue']`.",
        "Create a computed property `error` that runs the validation rules (if any) on the current value.",
        "The rules can be an object with keys like `required`, `minLength`, `email`, each being a function that returns an error message or null.",
        "Pass the rules from parent: `:rules=\"{ required: true, minLength: 3 }\"` and map to validator functions."
    ],
    "expectedOutput": "A working registration form using custom validated inputs.",
    "solutionCode": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n  <title>Custom Validated Input</title>\n  <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/vue@3/dist/vue.global.js\"></script>\n  <style>\n    .error { color: red; font-size: 0.8em; }\n    input.error { border: 1px solid red; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div id=\"app\">\n    <h2>Registration</h2>\n    <validated-input\n      v-model=\"form.username\"\n      label=\"Username\"\n      :rules=\"{ required: true, minLength: 3 }\"\n    />\n    <validated-input\n      v-model=\"form.email\"\n      label=\"Email\"\n      type=\"email\"\n      :rules=\"{ required: true, email: true }\"\n    />\n    <validated-input\n      v-model=\"form.password\"\n      label=\"Password\"\n      type=\"password\"\n      :rules=\"{ required: true, minLength: 6 }\"\n    />\n    <button @click=\"submit\" :disabled=\"!isFormValid\">Register</button>\n  </div>\n\n  <script>\n    const ValidatedInput = {\n      props: ['modelValue', 'label', 'rules', 'type'],\n      emits: ['update:modelValue'],\n      data() {\n        return { touched: false };\n      },\n      computed: {\n        error() {\n          if (!this.touched) return '';\n          const value = this.modelValue;\n          if (this.rules?.required && (!value || value.trim() === '')) {\n            return `${this.label} is required`;\n          }\n          if (this.rules?.minLength && value && value.length < this.rules.minLength) {\n            return `${this.label} must be at least ${this.rules.minLength} characters`;\n          }\n          if (this.rules?.email && value && !value.includes('@')) {\n            return `Please enter a valid email`;\n          }\n          return '';\n        }\n      },\n      template: `\n        <div>\n          <label>{{ label }}</label>\n          <input\n            :type=\"type || 'text'\"\n            :value=\"modelValue\"\n            @input=\"$emit('update:modelValue', $event.target.value)\"\n            @blur=\"touched = true\"\n            :class=\"{ error: error }\"\n          >\n          <div v-if=\"error\" class=\"error\">{{ error }}</div>\n        </div>\n      `\n    };\n\n    createApp({\n      components: { ValidatedInput },\n      data() {\n        return {\n          form: { username: '', email: '', password: '' },\n          errors: { username: '', email: '', password: '' }\n        };\n      },\n      computed: {\n        isFormValid() {\n          // We'll rely on the components' validation but need a way to know.\n          // Simple approach: manually validate again, or use a ref to components.\n          // Here we'll do a quick check on the form data.\n          const usernameValid = this.form.username && this.form.username.length >= 3;\n          const emailValid = this.form.email && this.form.email.includes('@');\n          const passwordValid = this.form.password && this.form.password.length >= 6;\n          return usernameValid && emailValid && passwordValid;\n        }\n      },\n      methods: {\n        submit() {\n          if (this.isFormValid) {\n            alert('Registered: ' + JSON.stringify(this.form));\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }).mount('#app');\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>"
}